leap71/PicoGKRuntime @ 0f26321c18ed (26.2): LatticeBeam::fSdvRoundCone renders
the wrong shape when one end sphere contains the other.

Proposal only. picovoxel, an unofficial community TypeScript/WebAssembly binding
of PicoGK (not affiliated with or endorsed by LEAP 71), avoids the defect by
rendering lattices through openvdb's tube-complex voxelizer by default; its
optional serial lattice path and the PicoGK C# binding still reach this code.

The defect. fSdvRoundCone implements the round-cone (tapered capsule) distance.
When the end spheres nest, |a - b| <= |r1 - r2|, the shape is the larger
sphere, but the formula computes a2 = l2 - rr * rr <= 0 and later takes
sqrtf(x2 * a2 * il2) of a negative product. For a beam from radius 6 mm to 1 mm
over 2 mm, the distance at the centre of the 6 mm sphere comes out as +1 mm
(outside).

The fix returns the distance to the larger sphere in that case, before the
round-cone algebra (and before 1.0f / l2, which is infinite for a zero-length
beam). openvdb's tube voxelizer makes the same decision for the same condition
(tools/impl/LevelSetTubesImpl.h, the `// ball` branch).

Output values: unchanged for non-nested beams (the new branch runs only when
a2 <= 0); changed for nested beams, which move to the correct shape.

Numeric check, 2026-09-27, Apple clang -O2, against Source/PicoGKLattice.h and
Source/PicoGKTypes.h at 0f26321c18ed; volume sampled at 0.05 mm by counting
negative field values:

  beam                          before                    after       exact
  r 6 -> 1 over 2 mm            657.83 mm^3, centre +1.00 904.82, -6.00  904.78
  r 1 -> 6 over 2 mm            785.93 mm^3               904.82         904.78
  r 3 -> 1 over 6 mm (control)  149.4410 mm^3             149.4410       -

The check program is upstream/picogkruntime-roundcone-nested-spheres-check.cpp
in the picovoxel repository. Rendered to voxels, the same r 6 -> 1 beam measured
84.21 mm^3 against the closed form's 904.78 mm^3 (-90.7%) in picovoxel's
WebAssembly build, with 160 tools::checkLevelSet violations
(test/tier2.test.mjs pins the direction of the difference).

Target file sha256 prefix: Source/PicoGKLattice.h d5aae62f9be8fdd2.
Applies with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0` to a pristine PicoGKRuntime 0f26321c tree, onto
it with patches/PicoGKRuntime/0003 applied, and onto it with 0001-0004 applied;
picogkruntime-tubecomplex-lattice.patch still applies on top.
Not applied by picovoxel's build; see upstream/README.md.

